WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.400
If you’re anything like me,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.560
you have lots of ambitious
plans for the future.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.160
I’ve got a whole series of
new books I want to write,

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.400
thousands more
videos to script.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.360
But guess what?

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.760
None of us may be able to do
any of the things we want to do

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.240
if we don't have our health.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.480
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.440
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.400
Today we have part two
of our series on resveratrol

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.480
and we start with a study

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:36.440
that shows that resveratrol appears to
triple the rate of age-related brain shrinkage.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:39.440
Does resveratrol help
with inflammation?

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.800
In humans, the evidence
of an anti-inflammatory effect

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.400
is sparse and conflicting.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.600
About half of the studies show

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.320
a modest
anti-inflammatory effect,

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.600
but the other half
failed to find any.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.240
The proof, however,
is in the pudding.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.800
What about clinical effects
on inflammatory disease?

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.800
In rats and mice,

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.640
resveratrol can help
ameliorate the effects

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.840
of experimentally-induced
periodontitis,

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.080
the inflammatory gum disease.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.120
However, it appears
to have no effect

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.880
on the progression
of chronic periodontitis

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.040
in human sufferers.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.680
Resveratrol may help with
the inflammatory bowel disease

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.200
ulcerative colitis, though.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.120
A pilot study
of 500 milligrams a day

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.800
of resveratrol for six weeks

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.480
resulted in significantly
decreased disease activity

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:23.440
and elevated quality of life
compared to placebo.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.640
What about inflammatory
joint disease?

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:27.640
One pilot study
of 500 milligrams a day

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:29.920
of resveratrol
for knee osteoarthritis

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.320
found a decrease in pain
within a month,

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:33.520
but there was no control group;

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:35.200
so, the change can't
really be attributed

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.040
to starting the supplements.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.720
However, a second pilot study,

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:41.240
a randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial,

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.480
found that the same dose
taken as an "add on"

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:46.680
to an anti-inflammatory drug
significantly improved

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.360
pain and function
within a month

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.800
in mild-to-moderate
knee osteoarthritis sufferers,

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:53.240
more than adding a placebo.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:55.600
The one clinical trial
of rheumatoid arthritis

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.120
had a control group,
but no placebo,

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:00.280
though there were
objective signs of improvement

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.400
in disease activity after
taking 1000 milligrams a day

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.240
for three months.

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:06.920
Resveratrol may also be
beneficial

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:09.240
to combat menopausal symptoms.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:12.360
Resveratrol has
some estrogenic activity.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.000
Although it doesn't appear
to help with hormonal migraines,

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.360
it does appear to help
with a couple symptoms of PCOS,

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.520
polycystic ovary syndrome.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:24.120
RESHAW—Resveratrol
for Healthy Ageing in Women—

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.520
is the longest study of effects

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:29.160
of resveratrol supplementation
in postmenopausal women.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.040
Those randomized
to 75 milligrams

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.360
of resveratrol twice a day

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.680
suffered significantly fewer
physical menopausal symptoms,

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.040
including aches and pains,

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:39.280
and a general improvement
in overall well-being

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.400
compared to placebo.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.520
The RESHAW study also looked
at bone loss prevention.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.200
Unfortunately,
though animal studies

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.000
show protective effects
on bone tissue,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.680
a meta-analysis
of human studies

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.080
on resveratrol supplementation
to improve bone quality

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:55.440
found no significant effect
on bone health markers

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.760
or bone mineral density

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:01.120
of the spine, hip,
or overall skeleton.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:04.760
A similar story was found
for cognitive effects.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.120
Most studies on resveratrol
for brain function

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.320
in animal models
show positive outcomes,

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.720
but meta-analyses
of human studies show

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:13.920
no significant effect
on memory,

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.560
processing speed,
executive function,

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.520
or global
cognitive performance,

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.480
which led reviewers to suggest
that resveratrol may be

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.840
a "cognitive enhancer
for mice only."

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:27.360
Most human cognition studies
found no effect

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.960
or mixed results—higher
performance on some tasks,

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:32.240
but lower performance on others,
compared to placebo,

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:34.640
resulting in
a "lack of interpretable

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.480
cognitive effects."

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.200
Some have suggested
the discrepancy

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.480
between the animal models
and the clinical data

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:42.720
is that the rodents
were massively dosed,

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.200
up to a gram per kilogram
of body weight a day,

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.680
which would be
like giving people

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:47.600
an entire bottle

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:51.200
of high-dose resveratrol
supplements at once.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.200
Or, ironically,
it could be the opposite,

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.360
where the doses researchers
gave people were too large.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:57.440
A dose-response study

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:59.400
found that human
cerebral blood flow

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.600
was maximally boosted

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.280
by the lowest dose
of resveratrol tested,

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:05.200
seventy-five milligrams a day.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.080
So, when the RESHAW study
was developed,

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.920
that was the dose they used,
given twice a day.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.280
RESHAW was primarily designed
to test the effects

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:14.600
of resveratrol
on cognitive performance.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:18.280
Interim analyses at 14 weeks
and a year looked promising,

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:20.640
leading the researchers
to conclude that their findings

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:22.480
"support the adoption
of resveratrol

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:24.080
as a low-cost,
effective intervention

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:25.400
to help counteract the age-

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.960
and menopause-related
accelerated cognitive decline

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.720
in our ageing population."

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.880
However, by the end
of the two-year study,

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.400
it's not clear
if the apparent benefit

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.520
in overall cognition

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:38.560
survives adjustment
for multiple comparisons,

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.240
meaning there were so many
cognitive outcomes tested

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:43.200
that the few treatment
differences

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:46.600
may well have arisen
through chance.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:50.040
What about cognitive benefit
for those who really need it?

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.120
Observational studies
find wine drinkers

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:54.240
tend to get less dementia,

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.560
but it's hard to disentangle
the social, cognitive,

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:57.720
and personality factors

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.640
that accompany
a wine drinking habit.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.800
So, researchers decided
to put resveratrol to the test

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:05.840
for Alzheimer's disease.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:08.160
A randomized double-blind,
placebo-controlled pilot

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.080
out of Cornell in 2006
kicked things off with a bang.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.960
Patients with mild-to-moderate
Alzheimer's disease

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:16.160
who were randomized
to a 5 milligram

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:18.280
resveratrol concoction
twice a day

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:20.520
ended up with significantly
better cognition

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.920
after three months
compared to placebo.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.840
There was a greater
than expected deterioration

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.320
in the placebo group, though,

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.640
suggesting that this may
have just been a fluke,

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:32.480
especially since an attempt
to replicate the study

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:35.960
with the same dose for a year
failed to find any effects

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:38.240
of statistical significance.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:41.760
Maybe the researchers just
didn't use a high enough dose?

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:42.800
More than a hundred patients

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.040
with mild to moderate
Alzheimer's

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:45.240
were randomized to placebo

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:47.400
or an escalating dose
of resveratrol

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.160
starting at a hundred times
the dose

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.720
of the previous study—
500 milligrams once a day

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:55.040
and ending at a 1000 milligrams
twice a day.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.760
After a year,

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:58.960
there were no significant
improvements in cognition

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:01.160
or the performance of activities
of daily living

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.360
compared to placebo.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:07.800
Instead, there was
a significant acceleration

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.120
of brain volume loss.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:11.440
At the end of the study,

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:14.080
there was triple
the brain volume loss

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:16.800
(3 percent versus 1 percent)
in the resveratrol group.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:18.760
And the only other randomized,
double-blind,

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:20.480
placebo-controlled trial to date

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:21.840
found the same thing:

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:23.440
no significant
cognitive benefits

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:27.800
and the same tripling
of age-related brain shrinkage.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:30.760
The authors tried to somehow
spin this as a positive,

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:34.400
like hey—maybe that's just
decreased brain swelling,

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.120
but as a team
of researchers wrote

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.680
in an understatement
of the year,

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:41.000
"It is difficult
to reconcile these effects

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.960
as potentially beneficial."

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:45.400
In our final story of the series,

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.440
we discover how
resveratrol supplements

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:51.360
may blunt some of the positive
effects of exercise training.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:52.480
If you do have a condition

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:54.840
that might benefit from
resveratrol supplementation,

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:57.360
like diabetic foot ulcers,
or ulcerative colitis,

00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:58.920
or menopausal pains,

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:01.160
and want to give resveratrol
a try,

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:04.240
are there any concerns,
aside from the cost,

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:06.360
which can exceed $10 a day?

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:09.320
Well, although a meta-analysis
of studies of resveratrol

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:12.000
found no overall effect
on LDL cholesterol levels,

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.120
a couple studies
found that resveratrol

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.560
sometimes increased LDL levels,

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.320
up to 25 percent over placebo.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:22.200
As cardiovascular disease
is by far the leading killer

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:24.000
of diabetics,

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.920
as well as other conditions
for which you might take it,

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:30.320
if you do try resveratrol,
please make sure

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:33.600
to have your cholesterol
closely monitored.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:35.920
The scientific literature
regarding resveratrol

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:38.520
and cardiovascular health
in general is said to be

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:41.680
"replete with conflicting
information and controversy."

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:42.720
There are no human studies

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:45.000
on cardiovascular disease
outcomes,

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.720
but an often-overlooked study

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:51.280
found that resveratrol caused
atherosclerosis in rabbits.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:52.560
The study, entitled

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:54.760
"Resveratrol promotes
atherosclerosis

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:57.000
in hypercholesterolemic
rabbits,"

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.040
found that the hardening
of the arteries of bunnies

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:03.000
fed dietary cholesterol
was worsened by resveratrol.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.960
But, negative or null findings
are often marginalized

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.760
by the resveratrol
research community;

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:09.880
so, you rarely hear about them.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:12.160
Though there are
no long-term safety data,

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:15.200
450 milligrams a day
has been considered a safe dose,

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.720
at least in the short term,
for a 60 kilogram person

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.120
(that's like 130 pounds),
but supplementation

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:22.960
at higher doses
could be potentially toxic.

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:26.120
Daily doses of resveratrol
in excess of a gram

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:29.080
commonly cause mild to moderate
gastrointestinal symptoms,

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:32.080
such as nausea, diarrhea,
abdominal pain,

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:35.080
as well as "anal itchiness."

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:36.680
Unexpected renal toxicity

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:38.600
with cases
of severe kidney failure

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:41.360
were noted
in a five-gram-a-day study,

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:43.160
but this was in the context
of a cancer

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:46.560
that is particularly hard
on the kidneys.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:49.000
Two studies, however, found
that so-called "safe" levels

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.280
of resveratrol
(at 150 to 250 milligrams a day)

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:54.240
may blunt
some of the positive effects

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:56.040
of exercise training.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:59.040
In rodents, resveratrol
supplementation decreases

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:00.320
cardiovascular risk factors

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:02.000
and improves
cardiovascular function

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.520
and physical capacity.

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:05.840
But, when it was
put to the test in older men

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:09.800
(with an average age of 65),
the exact opposite was found.

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:12.000
Specifically,
combining resveratrol

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.440
with athletic training
abolished the reduction

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:16.520
in blood pressure, cholesterol,
and triglycerides

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:18.600
normally associated
with exercise,

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:21.920
had a more artery-constricting
effect than a dilating one,

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:24.160
and led to a significantly
lower increase

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:26.360
in aerobic fitness.

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:29.560
Rodents on resveratrol get
enhanced exercise performance,

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:31.840
but, in people,
the resveratrol induced

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:35.360
a 45 percent lower increase
in maximum aerobic capacity

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:37.360
compared with those
taking a sugar pill.

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:38.600
For all their working out,

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:41.640
the resveratrol
was undercutting their efforts.

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:43.680
An apparent impairment
in peak aerobic power

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:45.360
was also noted in young men

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:47.560
following high-intensity
interval training

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:50.760
on resveratrol
compared to placebo.

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:53.360
A recent review
overreacted to these data

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.440
by suggesting "foods
containing resveratrol

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:58.080
should not be consumed
during exercise,"

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:00.840
but to even reach
the lower dose of 150 milligrams

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:02.600
you'd have to eat
more than like

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:05.320
a hundred pounds
of grapes a day.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:07.400
Though, I suppose
if you did manage to stuff

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:08.400
in a hundred pounds of grapes,

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:12.080
it might, indeed,
be a little impairing.

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:14.840
The exercise impairment
with resveratrol supplements

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:18.720
does make sense, though,
given its purported mechanism.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.460
Sirtuin activation
by resveratrol

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:22.720
is thought to occur
via the activation

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.960
of the body's fuel gauge, AMPK,

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:27.280
by interfering
with energy production

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:30.680
in the mitochondria powerplants
in our cells.

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:34.400
Mouse cells react by increasing
mitochondria to compensate,

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.640
but human cells
apparently do not;

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:39.680
so, the energy-dimming effect
of resveratrol

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:43.640
may explain why the effects
of exercise are impaired.

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:47.440
What works in animals may not
necessarily work in people.

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:50.880
Thus, concluded one review,
the hype regarding resveratrol

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.160
may "turn out to be
nothing more

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:54.920
than a sleight-of-hand
marketing device

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:58.120
using peer-reviewed, published,
non-human research

00:10:58.120 --> 00:10:59.360
as a cover."

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:02.560
Although some like Dr. Oz
have recommended resveratrol

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:05.040
as a life-extending
"miracle molecule,"

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:06.640
given that evidence-based
responses

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:08.320
are sparse-and-controversial

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:10.840
such "claims, innuendo,
and hyperbole"

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:14.120
are said to be "atrocious."

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:16.960
The fitness-blunting exercise
study of older adults

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:19.720
was supported in part
by a manufacturer

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:21.560
of resveratrol supplements.

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:23.760
To their credit,
the researchers responded

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:26.880
to an angry letter from
a supplement company consultant

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:30.520
that "it is our opinion
that we, as scientists,

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:33.160
have a responsibility
to report what we find

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:34.760
and not to twist our findings

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:38.318
to fit the commercial interests."
Unquote.

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:41.200
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:44.600
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:47.520
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:51.960
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:56.720
If you want to see any graphs, charts,
graphics, images, or studies mentioned here,

00:11:56.720 --> 00:12:00.080
please go to the Nutrition Facts
Podcast landing page.

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:02.220
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:06.560
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite for each of these topics.

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:11.320
My latest book, “How Not to Age” has
been out for about half a year now.

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:14.520
Check it out from your
local public library.

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:16.960
And of course, all the proceeds
I receive of the sales

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.800
of all my books goes
directly to charity.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:23.280
NutritionFacts.org is a nonprofit,
science-based public service,

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:25.360
where you can sign up
for free daily updates

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:29.640
on the latest in nutrition research
via bite-sized videos and articles.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:31.360
Everything on the
website is free.

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:32.240
There’s no ads,

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:33.880
no corporate sponsorships,
no kickbacks.

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:36.760
It’s strictly non-commercial.
I’m not selling anything.

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:40.000
I just put it up as a public service,
as a labor of love,

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:41.920
as a tribute to
my grandmother,

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:46.360
whose own life was saved
with evidence-based nutrition.

